{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health.md | sed -n '1,500p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Story 2: Inspect Domain - Overview and Health\n     2\t\n     3\t### Summary\n     4\t<!-- Jira: Summary field -->\n     5\tCreate the inspect domain with read-only overview and derivation health reports.\n     6\t\n     7\t### Description\n     8\t<!-- Jira: Description field -->\n     9\t**User Profile:** The operator audits threads from the CLI; agents inside a harness use the same reads mid-task.\n    10\t\n    11\t**Objective:** Report thread composition, derivation state, repair preview, queue visibility, and rebuild visibility without changing state.\n    12\t\n    13\t**Scope In:** `inspect.overview`, `inspect.health`, `lhc inspect overview`, `lhc inspect health`, owner-surface composition, fixture extension for mutation-in-flight states.\n    14\t\n    15\t**Scope Out:** Repair execution and mutations remain Feature 2 behavior. Inspect reports and previews; it never repairs, requeues, writes rows, transitions state, moves boundaries, derives forms, or invokes a provider.\n    16\t\n    17\t**Dependencies:** Built Epic 01 and Epic 02 surfaces. Epic 03 status/view shapes are consumed where overview reports active-view summary.\n    18\t\n    19\t### Acceptance Criteria\n    20\t<!-- Jira: Acceptance Criteria field -->\n    21\t- **AC-1.1**: `inspect.overview` returns, in one read-only call: thread identity and metadata; event count and order span; message counts (total visible, by kind, deleted counted separately) with visible token sum; turn counts (open, closed); chunk count and closed-but-unchunked turn count; derivation counts by state (pending, retrying, failed, blocked, ready); active-view summary (viewId, createdAt, compactPoint, coveredFrom) or null when never compacted; visibility boundary position and current zone token sum.\n    22\t\n    23\t- **AC-1.2**: Counts honor the deleted contract: deleted messages appear only in the deleted count — excluded from visible counts, kind breakdowns, and token sums; event counts are unaffected (the record retains everything).\n    24\t\n    25\t- **AC-1.3**: Every thread shape reports cleanly: fresh-empty, mid-first-turn, never-compacted, compacted, mid-rebuild. Absent pieces report as zeros or null — never omitted fields, never shape errors.\n    26\t\n    27\t- **TC-1.1** (AC-1.1, AC-1.3): Overview shape variants: fresh-empty, mid-first-turn, never-compacted-with-record, compacted, and mid-rebuild all return the full shape with absent pieces as zeros/nulls. The compacted tool-heavy fixture asserts exact expected counts (messages by kind, turns, chunks, derivation states, view summary, boundary).\n    28\t\n    29\t- **TC-1.2** (AC-1.2): Delete one message; overview → visible count and token sum drop, deleted count = 1, kind breakdown excludes it, event count unchanged.\n    30\t\n    31\t- **AC-1.4**: The overview is a pure read: no work items created, no state changed, repeated calls with no intervening writes return identical results.\n    32\t\n    33\t- **TC-1.3** (AC-1.4): Overview twice with no writes between → deep-equal results; no `work_item` rows created; zero provider calls.\n    34\t\n    35\t- **AC-4.1**: `inspect.health` aggregates across owners — counts by owner, form kind, and state (ready, pending, retrying, failed, blocked) — assembled entirely from the owners' report surfaces, never from direct `derived_form` or `work_item` reads.\n    36\t\n    37\t- **AC-4.2**: Failures carry actionable detail: subject id, form kind, reason, attempts, last error — enough to decide and target a requeue without raw SQL.\n    38\t\n    39\t- **AC-4.3**: The report previews repair: which forms a requeue pass would touch (failed and not blocked), reported and never executed.\n    40\t\n    41\t- **AC-4.4**: Rebuild visibility: after an edit or delete, health shows the cascade-cleared forms as pending with their queued work visible; after the queue drains, the same forms report ready. Two reads bracket a rebuild.\n    42\t\n    43\t- **AC-4.5**: Live queue visibility: queued and claimed work counts from the owners' queue detail, consistent with the state counts in the same report.\n    44\t\n    45\t- **TC-4.1** (AC-4.1, AC-4.5): Fixture with manufactured mixed states (ready, failed-transient, failed-permanent, blocked, pending) → exact counts per owner, kind, and state; queue section consistent with pending counts.\n    46\t\n    47\t- **TC-4.2** (AC-4.2, AC-4.3): Failed and blocked forms present → failure detail exact (subject, form, reason, attempts); repair preview lists exactly the failed-not-blocked set.\n    48\t\n    49\t- **TC-4.3** (AC-4.4): Edit a mid-thread message → health shows the cascade's cleared set pending with queued work (exact subjects per the cascade contract); `drainSettled` → same set ready; nothing outside the cascade changed state.\n    50\t\n    51\t### Technical Design\n    52\t<!-- Jira: Technical Notes or sub-section of Description -->\n    53\t#### Architecture Context\n    54\t\n    55\tThis story creates the inspect domain and its shared report shapes. `overview` composes list/status/describe reads into counts and summaries; `health` composes owner report surfaces and queue detail into state counts, failure detail, and repair preview.\n    56\t\n    57\tInspect is a pure consumer. It imports owner surfaces, owns no tables, performs no provider work, and reports repair targets without executing repair.\n    58\t\n    59\t#### Build Strategy\n    60\t\n    61\tStrategy: tdd-lite\n    62\t\n    63\tReason:\n    64\t- The story spans multiple owner surfaces and establishes the read-only delta helper used by later chunks.\n    65\t\n    66\tRisk Reminders:\n    67\t- Count correctness comes from list reads, not direct table reads.\n    68\t- Health must stay on owner report surfaces and queue detail.\n    69\t- The mutation-in-flight fixture must reach states through production mutation/drain behavior, not hand-written derived rows.\n    70\t\n    71\t#### Implementation Targets\n    72\t\n    73\t| Area | Files / Modules |\n    74\t|------|-----------------|\n    75\t| Inspect surface | `src/domains/inspect/index.ts` |\n    76\t| Inspect internals | `src/domains/inspect/internal/overview.ts`, `src/domains/inspect/internal/health.ts` |\n    77\t| Shared shapes | `src/shared/inspect.ts` |\n    78\t| CLI | `src/cli/inspect.ts` |\n    79\t| SDK export | `src/sdk.ts` |\n    80\t| Tests | `test/inspect-overview.test.ts`, `test/inspect-health.test.ts`, read-only delta helper in the test support area |\n    81\t\n    82\t#### Design References\n    83\t\n    84\t- [tech-design.md §Context](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:6), lines 6-22\n    85\t- [tech-design.md §System View](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:24), lines 24-52\n    86\t- [tech-design.md §Module Boundaries](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:54), lines 54-98\n    87\t- [tech-design.md §Flow 1: Overview](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:104), lines 104-123\n    88\t- [tech-design.md §Flow 4: Health](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:143), lines 143-146\n    89\t- [tech-design.md §Interface Definitions](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:151), lines 151-213\n    90\t- [tech-design.md §Testing Strategy](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:215), lines 215-217\n    91\t- [test-plan.md §Architecture-Risk Tests](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md:42), lines 42-50\n    92\t- [test-plan.md §Chunk Red/Green Detail](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md:56), lines 56-64\n    93\t\n    94\t#### Test Mapping\n    95\t\n    96\t| TC | Test File / Check | Test Description |\n    97\t|----|-------------------|------------------|\n    98\t| TC-1.1 | `test/inspect-overview.test.ts :: full shape variants` | Fresh-empty, mid-first-turn, never-compacted-with-record, compacted, and mid-rebuild return full shape and exact fixture counts. |\n    99\t| TC-1.2 | `test/inspect-overview.test.ts :: deleted accounting` | Deleting one message changes visible/deleted/kind/token counts while event count stays unchanged. |\n   100\t| TC-1.3 | `test/inspect-overview.test.ts :: purity` | Repeated overview reads are deep-equal, read-only delta stays green, and provider calls remain zero. |\n   101\t| TC-4.1 | `test/inspect-health.test.ts :: counts + queue consistency` | Mixed-state fixture returns exact counts per owner/kind/state and queue consistency. |\n   102\t| TC-4.2 | `test/inspect-health.test.ts :: failure detail + preview` | Failed entries expose reason/attempts/last error and preview exactly failed-not-blocked forms. |\n   103\t| TC-4.3 | `test/inspect-health.test.ts :: rebuild bracket` | Edit creates pending queued cascade set; after drain the same set is ready and disjoint forms are untouched. |\n   104\t\n   105\t#### Architecture-Risk Tests\n   106\t\n   107\t| Risk | Test File / Check | Test Description | Why AC/TC Mapping Alone Would Miss It |\n   108\t|------|-------------------|------------------|---------------------------------------|\n   109\t| Inspect writes while reporting | Shared read-only delta helper | Snapshot queued work, boundary/zone, view identity, and record counts before/after every new read. | Shape assertions do not prove absence of side effects. |\n   110\t| Health reads owner tables directly | `check-boundaries` plus Epic 04 source check | Forbid cross-domain internals and raw SQL references to other domains from `domains/inspect/**`. | A direct SQL implementation could match output while violating inspect ownership. |\n   111\t| Provider use leaks into reads | Suite-wide throwing-provider assertion | New read operations succeed under throwing provider config. | Fixture prep may use deterministic provider; report operations themselves must not. |\n   112\t\n   113\t#### Technical Notes\n   114\t\n   115\t- Overview reads `listEvents`, `listMessages({ includeDeleted: true })`, `listTurns`, `listChunks`, `status`, and `describe`, then normalizes absent sections to zero/null.\n   116\t- Health reads owner reports and queued-work detail; `repairPreview` reports failed-not-blocked forms only.\n   117\t- No migration, new table, or new index ships in this story.\n   118\t\n   119\t#### Anti-Shim Requirements\n   120\t\n   121\t- Mutation-in-flight fixture states must be reached through intake, mutation, and partial drain behavior.\n   122\t- Do not add count-only surfaces or table reads for overview counts.\n   123\t- Do not execute repair or requeue from `health`.\n   124\t\n   125\t#### Production Path Proof\n   126\t\n   127\t- Entrypoint: `inspect.overview`, `inspect.health`, `lhc inspect overview`, `lhc inspect health`.\n   128\t- Registration/default path: `src/sdk.ts` exposes the inspect namespace; `src/cli/inspect.ts` routes commands to SDK calls.\n   129\t- Evidence: default-suite overview/health tests plus read-only delta helper; CLI parity is covered in the lifecycle/process story.\n   130\t\n   131\t#### Verification\n   132\t\n   133\t- Targeted: `pnpm verify`\n   134\t- Story gate: `pnpm verify`\n   135\t- Epic/process gate: `LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1 pnpm verify-all`\n   136\t\n   137\t#### Spec Deviations\n   138\t\n   139\tNone.\n   140\t\n   141\t### Definition of Done\n   142\t<!-- Jira: Definition of Done or Acceptance Criteria footer -->\n   143\t- `inspect.overview` returns the full overview shape for fresh, mid-turn, never-compacted, compacted, and mid-rebuild threads.\n   144\t- Overview count behavior honors the deleted-message contract and pure-read invariant.\n   145\t- `inspect.health` composes owner report surfaces for counts, failures, repair preview, and queue visibility.\n   146\t- Rebuild visibility is covered before and after drain.\n   147\t- CLI overview/health JSON matches SDK results.\n   148\t- TC-1.1 through TC-1.3 and TC-4.1 through TC-4.3 pass with one primary owner in this story.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md | sed -n '1,500p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Epic 04: Inspection — Tech Design\n     2\t\n     3\t**Epic:** `epic.md` (23 ACs / 17 TCs) · **Tech arch:** `../01-tech-arch.md` · **Test plan:** `test-plan.md`\n     4\t**Inherits:** Epic 01–03 technical world — storage/transaction rules, error model, `OpResult`, verification tiers, process-suite accounting, CLI conventions. Nothing re-stated here that those designs pin; this document covers what Epic 04 adds.\n     5\t\n     6\t## Context\n     7\t\n     8\tThe last epic of the v1 PRD, and the smallest: no migration, no new tables, no derivations, no provider use, no new algorithms. Four read surfaces and a lifecycle exercise. The design problem is not mechanism — it is *composition discipline*: every report assembles other domains' surfaces without touching their tables, and where a report describes another surface's output (`loadCost` vs `pull`), the design makes agreement structural rather than tested-into-existence (the materialize parity-by-construction pattern, reused).\n     9\t\n    10\tThe second design problem is the dependency posture: this epic consumes Epic 03's surfaces, which finished building days before this design. The epic's handoff gate requires the deviation check below.\n    11\t\n    12\t## Spec Validation\n    13\t\n    14\tDesigned from the epic; issues found and resolved during design:\n    15\t\n    16\t| # | Issue | Resolution | Status |\n    17\t|---|-------|-----------|--------|\n    18\t| 1 | **Handoff gate (epic Assumptions):** Epic 02/03 final deviation tables vs the contracts this epic consumes | Reviewed all recorded deviations (Epic 02 impl log; Epic 03 impl log: `ViewProfileOverride[]` config typing, `view_boundary` strftime seed, `ViewCompactParams` nested partial, additive error codes, sweep-absent literal superseded by Story 3). None alter consumed shapes: `ViewStatus`, `PullResult`, `thread_view`/`thread_view_band`/`view_boundary` DDL, `messages.report`/`turns.report`, `FormReportEntry`, `MessageRecord.forms` all match spec as built. One *favorable* drift: Epic 02's AC-4.7 ruling attached `forms` to message reads (built for this consumer), so Flow 3's join is thinner than the epic assumed | Gate PASSED — recorded here |\n    19\t| 2 | AC-1.1 needs counts (events, messages by kind, tokens) that no surface exposes as counts; inspect may not read tables directly; epic sanctions only one surface addition (`describe`) | Overview composes *list* reads (`listEvents`, `listMessages`, `listTurns`, `listChunks`) and counts in inspect. Cost is linear in thread size — acceptable at v1 scale (NFR allows thread-proportional reads). Count-only surface ops are a deferred optimization, not a v1 need | Resolved — composition, no new surfaces |\n    20\t| 3 | Epic Data Contracts leave list-option names to tech design | Pinned: `{ from?, to?, limit?, includeDeleted? }` — `from`/`to` are source-event-order bounds (reports name `sourceEventOrder`, so drill-down uses the coordinate the operator already holds), `limit` caps count after bounds | Resolved — DD-3 |\n    21\t| 4 | AC-2.3 equality (`loadCost` totals what pull serves) could be a fragile re-implementation of pull's costing | `inspect.view` *invokes* `threadView.pull` through the surface and measures its output — parity by construction; the TC's independent leg runs a second pull in the test and re-measures. Same pattern as Epic 03's materialize | Resolved — DD-4 |\n    22\t| 5 | TC-5.x suite placement left open by epic (TD question 5) | TC-5.1–5.3 default suite (in-process, deterministic, fast); TC-5.4 process suite (spawned CLI). The epic's lean (\"TC-5.1 likely default\") extended after checking runtimes: replay + teardown legs spawn nothing | Resolved — DD-8 |\n    23\t\n    24\t## System View\n    25\t\n    26\t```\n    27\t                    ┌─────────────── inspect (NEW) ───────────────┐\n    28\t                    │  overview()      view()       health()      │\n    29\t                    └───┬─────┬─────────┬──┬───────────┬──────────┘\n    30\t                        │     │         │  │           │\n    31\t        ┌───────────────┘     │         │  └───────┐   └────────┐\n    32\t        ▼                     ▼         ▼          ▼            ▼\n    33\t   threads.resolve      intake-stream  thread-view  messages.report\n    34\t   listThreads          .listEvents    .describe(NEW) turns.report\n    35\t                                       .pull        .listQueuedWork\n    36\t                        messages.listMessages(+opts)\n    37\t                        messages.show (NEW)          turns.listTurns/listChunks\n    38\t```\n    39\t\n    40\t`inspect` sits at the top of the domain graph: pure consumer, imports five surfaces, nothing imports it except `sdk.ts` and `cli/`. No cycles — unlike Epic 03's sanctioned intake→thread-view cycle, this addition is acyclic by construction. `check-boundaries` gains the domain with no exception entries.\n    41\t\n    42\t### External Contracts (consumed, as built)\n    43\t\n    44\t| Contract | Source | Used by |\n    45\t|----------|--------|---------|\n    46\t| `listEvents` → ordered `EventRecord[]` | intake-stream (E01) | overview (count, span) |\n    47\t| `listMessages` → `MessageRecord[]` with `forms?` attached | messages (E01 + E02 AC-4.7) | overview, list/show |\n    48\t| `report(ref, {messageId?})` → `FormReportEntry[]` (queue join) | messages/turns (E02) | health, show |\n    49\t| `listTurns` / `listChunks` / `listQueuedWork` | turns (E01/E02) | overview, health |\n    50\t| `status` → `ViewStatus` | thread-view (E03) | overview (visibility, derivation counts) |\n    51\t| `pull` → `PullResult` | thread-view (E03) | view (loadCost by construction) |\n    52\t| `thread_view` row + bands (storage, in-domain) | thread-view (E03) | `describe` only |\n    53\t\n    54\t## Module Boundaries\n    55\t\n    56\t### Placement\n    57\t\n    58\t```\n    59\tsrc/\n    60\t  domains/\n    61\t    inspect/\n    62\t      index.ts          ← NEW surface: overview, view, health\n    63\t      internal/\n    64\t        overview.ts     ← compose counts from list reads\n    65\t        view-report.ts  ← describe + pull → ViewContentsReport\n    66\t        health.ts       ← report joins → HealthReport\n    67\t    thread-view/\n    68\t      index.ts          ← gains describe() (read-only, ~30 lines)\n    69\t    messages/\n    70\t      index.ts          ← listMessages gains opts; gains show()\n    71\t  shared/\n    72\t    inspect.ts          ← NEW: InspectOverview, ViewContentsReport, HealthReport shapes\n    73\t  cli/\n    74\t    inspect.ts          ← NEW: lhc inspect overview|view|health\n    75\t    messages-read.ts    ← NEW: lhc messages list|show (mutations stay in messages-mutate.ts)\n    76\t  sdk.ts                ← gains inspect namespace; threadView.describe; messages.show/list opts\n    77\t```\n    78\t\n    79\t### Module Responsibility Matrix\n    80\t\n    81\t| Module | Owns | Must NOT own |\n    82\t|--------|------|--------------|\n    83\t| `inspect/index.ts` + internal | Report assembly, counting, shaping | Any table read, any write, any provider call, any derivation interpretation beyond the owners' reported states |\n    84\t| `thread-view/describe` | Exposing stored view row (arrangement, gaps, config, source state) | Recomputing anything; mutating; reading the record |\n    85\t| `messages/show` | Single-record read (full blocks) + `report(messageId)` composition | View-form shortening (show returns the record — full tool results, never boundary-shortened) |\n    86\t| `messages/listMessages` opts | Bounds, limit, deleted filter | Default-including deleted (audit is opt-in) |\n    87\t| `cli/inspect.ts`, `cli/messages-read.ts` | argv → SDK → JSON stdout | Any logic beyond arg mapping (CLI parity is structural: same code path as SDK) |\n    88\t\n    89\tDesign decisions:\n    90\t\n    91\t- **DD-1 (describe placement):** `describe` lives in thread-view because the stored view row is thread-view's table; inspect consuming it through the surface keeps the must-not-own rule airtight. Absent view → `ok` with `null`, mirroring `status`'s never-compacted behavior.\n    92\t- **DD-2 (show composes report):** `show` = internal single-message read (same store read as `listMessages`, by id, full blocks) + `messages.report(ref, {messageId})` for the queue-joined forms. No new join machinery; `FormReportEntry` is the forms shape `show` returns.\n    93\t- **DD-3 (list options):** `{ from?, to?, limit?, includeDeleted? }`, bounds in source event order. Existing callers unaffected (opts optional, default behavior unchanged: all visible messages).\n    94\t- **DD-4 (loadCost by construction):** `view-report.ts` calls `describe` (stored bands: entries, gaps, config, stored token counts) and `pull` (served messages). `loadCost.bandTokens` = sum of stored band counts; `loadCost.tailTokens` = estimator over pull's tail messages (band-absent entries); `total` = sum. Pull is the single costing authority for the tail — AC-2.2's boundary-aware shortening is inherited, not re-implemented.\n    95\t- **DD-5 (overview's view section):** composed from `status` (boundary, zone, derivation counts, view health) + `describe` (viewId, createdAt, compactPoint, coveredFrom) — both already exist; overview adds no view logic.\n    96\t- **DD-6 (read-only, structurally tested):** the architecture-risk test snapshots observable state (work-item rows via `listQueuedWork`/reports, boundary position via `status`, view identity via `describe`, event/message counts) before and after every inspect/describe/show/list call and asserts deep equality. Read-only is asserted as absence-of-delta, not absence-of-write-code.\n    97\t- **DD-7 (no migration):** schema terminal at v6. The one index temptation (message kind counts) is declined — counts come from list reads (Spec Validation #2); if profiling ever demands an index, that is a v7 proposal.\n    98\t- **DD-8 (suite placement):** TC-5.1–5.3 default suite; TC-5.4 process suite. The lifecycle script is a shared fixture helper (`test/fixtures/lifecycle.ts`) both suites drive, so the spawned leg replays the same sequence rather than a re-described one.\n    99\t\n   100\t## Storage\n   101\t\n   102\tNone. No tables, no migration, no new indexes (DD-7). The only storage *read* this epic adds is `describe`'s in-domain read of `thread_view` / `thread_view_band` / `view_boundary`, all Epic 03 tables.\n   103\t\n   104\t## Flow-by-Flow Design\n   105\t\n   106\t### Flow 1: Overview\n   107\t\n   108\t`overview(ref)`: resolve thread (registry metadata) → `listEvents` (count, first/last order) → `listMessages({includeDeleted: true})` (visible/deleted split, kind counts, visible token sum — deleted detected per the read contract's flag) → `listTurns` (open/closed counts) → `listChunks` (count; unchunked = closed turns minus chunk-member turns) → `status` + `describe` (derivation counts, visibility, view summary). Each piece independent; fresh-empty, mid-first-turn, never-compacted-with-record, compacted, and mid-rebuild shapes fall out of the same composition path: absent pieces are zeros/nulls; no shape-specific branch is allowed except normalizing null sections.\n   109\t\n   110\tWorked example (compacted fixture, abridged):\n   111\t\n   112\t```json\n   113\t{\n   114\t  \"thread\": { \"id\": \"th_…\", \"createdAt\": \"…\" },\n   115\t  \"events\": { \"count\": 412, \"span\": { \"first\": 1, \"last\": 412 } },\n   116\t  \"messages\": { \"visible\": 187, \"byKind\": { \"user_prompt\": 14, \"assistant_text\": 41, \"tool_call\": 66, \"tool_result\": 64, \"assistant_thinking\": 2 }, \"deleted\": 2, \"visibleTokens\": 96342 },\n   117\t  \"turns\": { \"open\": 0, \"closed\": 14 },\n   118\t  \"chunks\": { \"count\": 4, \"unchunkedTurns\": 2 },\n   119\t  \"derivation\": { \"ready\": 118, \"pending\": 3, \"retrying\": 1, \"failed\": 2, \"blocked\": 0 },\n   120\t  \"view\": { \"viewId\": \"v391\", \"createdAt\": \"…\", \"compactPoint\": 391, \"coveredFrom\": 12 },\n   121\t  \"visibility\": { \"boundaryPosition\": 398, \"zoneTokens\": 18204 }\n   122\t}\n   123\t```\n   124\t\n   125\t### Flow 2: View Contents Report\n   126\t\n   127\t```\n   128\tinspect.view ──► threadView.describe ──► stored arrangement/gaps/config/band tokens/source state\n   129\t      │\n   130\t      └────────► threadView.pull ──► served messages\n   131\t                      │\n   132\t                      ├─ band entries → cross-check count only (arrangement is describe's)\n   133\t                      └─ tail entries → estimator → tailTokens (as served: short forms short)\n   134\tloadCost = { bandTokens: Σ stored, tailTokens: measured, total: sum }\n   135\t```\n   136\t\n   137\tNever-compacted: `describe` → null ⇒ `meta: null`, bands empty, whole pull output is tail, parity contract unchanged (AC-2.4). The report never recomputes selection, rendering, or boundary state — stored snapshot + live pull are the only sources (AC-2.1's \"not recomputed\" is structural).\n   138\t\n   139\t### Flow 3: Message Listing and Show\n   140\t\n   141\t`listMessages(ref, opts)`: existing read + WHERE bounds on `source_event_order`, LIMIT, deleted filter (default excluded; `includeDeleted` includes flagged). `show(ref, messageId)`: by-id read, full blocks verbatim from the record, `deleted` flag honest, forms from `report({messageId})`. Not-found → `message_not_found` (existing code). Deleted + show → `ok` with flagged record (AC-3.3: audit, never not-found).\n   142\t\n   143\t### Flow 4: Health\n   144\t\n   145\t`health(ref)`: `messages.report` + `turns.report` (full, not-ready included) + `listQueuedWork` both owners. Compose: counts by owner/kind/state from report entries' states; `failures[]` from `failed`/`blocked` entries (reason, attempts, lastError off `FormReportEntry`); `repairPreview[]` = failed-and-not-blocked subjects (reported, never requeued — AC-4.3); `queue` = queued/claimed counts from the live-item joins, consistent by construction with the same entries' states (AC-4.5). Rebuild visibility (AC-4.4) is two health calls bracketing a drain — no new mechanism, the cascade's pending states simply show.\n   146\t\n   147\t### Flow 5: Lifecycle Exercise\n   148\t\n   149\tScripted in `test/fixtures/lifecycle.ts`: phases named `create | intake | drain | status | compact1 | pull1 | inspect1 | mutate | rebuild | health2 | compact2 | pull2 | materialize`. Each phase returns its results to the driving test; checkpoint assertions live in the test, not the script. Teardown leg (TC-5.3) re-creates the SDK between named phase groups using the same script with a `freshSdk` hook. Receipt-vs-health cross-check (AC-5.2): `compact2`'s receipt sweep section against the `health2` snapshot taken immediately before — field-level equality on the failed/requeued sets.\n   150\t\n   151\t## Interface Definitions\n   152\t\n   153\t`src/shared/inspect.ts` (load-bearing shapes; field comments carry AC refs in source):\n   154\t\n   155\t```typescript\n   156\texport interface InspectOverview {\n   157\t  thread: { id: string; createdAt: string; metadata?: Record<string, string> };\n   158\t  events: { count: number; span: { first: number; last: number } | null };\n   159\t  messages: { visible: number; byKind: Record<string, number>; deleted: number; visibleTokens: number };\n   160\t  turns: { open: number; closed: number };\n   161\t  chunks: { count: number; unchunkedTurns: number };\n   162\t  derivation: { ready: number; pending: number; retrying: number; failed: number; blocked: number };\n   163\t  view: { viewId: string; createdAt: string; compactPoint: number; coveredFrom: number } | null;\n   164\t  visibility: { boundaryPosition: number; zoneTokens: number };\n   165\t}\n   166\t\n   167\texport interface ViewContentsReport {\n   168\t  meta: { viewId: string; createdAt: string; profile: string | null;\n   169\t          config: { lowerBound: number; percentages: Record<string, number> };\n   170\t          compactPoint: number; coveredFrom: number } | null;\n   171\t  bands: Array<{ band: Band; entries: Array<{ subjectKind: \"chunk\" | \"turn\"; subjectId: string;\n   172\t          formUsed: string; degraded: boolean }>; storedTokens: number }>;\n   173\t  gaps: Array<{ band: Band; subjectId: string; reason: string }>;\n   174\t  tail: { messageCount: number; tokens: number };          // as served (AC-2.2)\n   175\t  loadCost: { bandTokens: number; tailTokens: number; total: number }; // = pull (AC-2.3)\n   176\t  sourceState: { maxEventOrder: number; formCounts: Record<string, number> }; // provenance verbatim (AC-2.5)\n   177\t}\n   178\t\n   179\texport interface HealthReport {\n   180\t  owners: Array<{ owner: \"messages\" | \"turns\"; kind: string;\n   181\t          counts: { ready: number; pending: number; retrying: number; failed: number; blocked: number } }>;\n   182\t  failures: Array<{ owner: string; subjectKind: string; subjectId: string; form: string;\n   183\t          reason: string; attempts: number; lastError?: string }>;\n   184\t  repairPreview: Array<{ owner: string; subjectKind: string; subjectId: string; form: string }>;\n   185\t  queue: { queued: number; claimed: number };\n   186\t}\n   187\t```\n   188\t\n   189\tSurface signatures:\n   190\t\n   191\t```typescript\n   192\t// inspect\n   193\toverview(ref: ThreadRef): Promise<OpResult<InspectOverview>>;\n   194\tview(ref: ThreadRef): Promise<OpResult<ViewContentsReport>>;\n   195\thealth(ref: ThreadRef): Promise<OpResult<HealthReport>>;\n   196\t// thread-view addition\n   197\tdescribe(ref: ThreadRef): Promise<OpResult<StoredView | null>>;   // StoredView mirrors the row: id, createdAt, compactPoint, coveredFrom, profileName, config, arrangement, gaps, sourceState, bands (band → storedTokens)\n   198\t// messages additions\n   199\tlistMessages(ref: ThreadRef, opts?: { from?: number; to?: number; limit?: number; includeDeleted?: boolean }): Promise<OpResult<MessageRecord[]>>;\n   200\tshow(ref: ThreadRef, messageId: string): Promise<OpResult<MessageDetail>>;  // MessageRecord (full blocks, deleted flag) + forms: FormReportEntry[]\n   201\t```\n   202\t\n   203\tCLI grammar (JSON stdout, existing error classes, exit conventions inherited):\n   204\t\n   205\t```\n   206\tlhc inspect overview --thread <ref>\n   207\tlhc inspect view     --thread <ref>\n   208\tlhc inspect health   --thread <ref>\n   209\tlhc messages list    --thread <ref> [--from <n>] [--to <n>] [--limit <n>] [--include-deleted]\n   210\tlhc messages show    --thread <ref> --message-id <id>\n   211\t```\n   212\t\n   213\tError codes: no additions. `thread_not_found`, `message_not_found`, `caller_error` (bad bounds: `from > to`, `limit < 1`), `state_corruption`, `system_error` — all existing.\n   214\t\n   215\t## Testing Strategy\n   216\t\n   217\tInherited wholesale from Epics 01–03: real temp SQLite, no mocks anywhere but the provider seam (unused here beyond fixture prep), default + process suites, zero-provider assertion extended to all inspect/show/list/describe operations. New emphasis — the **read-only delta assert** (DD-6) is this epic's architecture-risk centerpiece: every new operation runs under a before/after observable-state snapshot in one shared helper. Direct table-read prevention is static: `check-boundaries` forbids cross-domain internal imports, and this epic adds a source check that `domains/inspect/**` contains no raw SQL table-name access to other domains' tables. Test files: `inspect-overview.test.ts`, `inspect-view.test.ts`, `messages-read.test.ts`, `inspect-health.test.ts`, `lifecycle.test.ts`, `cli-process-inspect.test.ts` (process suite). Full TC mapping, fixture extensions, and Red/Green detail: `test-plan.md`.\n   218\t\n   219\t## Work Breakdown\n   220\t\n   221\tStory chunks follow the epic's four stories; per-chunk Red/Green and counts in the test plan.\n   222\t\n   223\t| Chunk | Story | Builds | Risk concentration |\n   224\t|-------|-------|--------|--------------------|\n   225\t| 1 | S1 Message reads | list opts, show, `cli/messages-read.ts` | Bounds semantics; deleted default; show returning record-not-view forms |\n   226\t| 2 | S2 Inspect domain | surface + overview + health, `shared/inspect.ts`, `cli/inspect.ts`, fixture mutation-states extension | Count correctness vs fixture ground truth; health composition staying on surfaces |\n   227\t| 3 | S3 View report | `describe`, `view-report.ts` | Parity-by-construction wiring; never-compacted nulls |\n   228\t| 4 | S4 Lifecycle | `lifecycle.ts` script + 4 TC legs | Checkpoint ordering; receipt-vs-health equality; teardown continuity |\n   229\t\n   230\tSequencing: 1 → 2 → 3 → 4 (3 needs Epic 03 storage live — already landed; 4 needs 1–3).\n   231\t\n   232\t## Open Questions\n   233\t\n   234\tNone blocking. Deferred items: count-only surface ops if thread scale ever makes overview's list-composition measurable (Spec Validation #2); message search (post-v1, PRD-recorded).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
