{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_49","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/team-impl-log.md | sed -n '1,500p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Team Impl Log — Epic 04: Inspection\n     2\t\n     3\tState: STORY_ACTIVE\n     4\tSpec-pack root: /Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection\n     5\tCurrent Story: 02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health\n     6\tCurrent Phase: implement (story-orchestrate)\n     7\t\n     8\t## Run Configuration\n     9\t\n    10\t- Date: 2026-06-12\n    11\t- Caller harness: Claude Code (Fable 5) acting as impl-lead.\n    12\t- Primary harness: claude-code. Secondary harness probe: codex-cli 0.139.0 available.\n    13\t- Defaults table applied: \"Codex available\" (operations/31-provider-resolution.md), no deviations.\n    14\t- Roles: story_lead_provider=codex gpt-5.5 high; story_implementor=claude-fable-5 medium; quick_fixer=claude-opus-4-8 xhigh; story_verifier=codex gpt-5.5 xhigh; epic-reviewer-1=claude-fable-5 xhigh; epic-reviewer-2=codex gpt-5.5 xhigh; epic_reverifier=claude-fable-5 xhigh.\n    15\t- Self-review passes: 3 (default).\n    16\t- Degraded-diversity: none (Codex available).\n    17\t- Prompt inserts: both absent (non-blocking).\n    18\t\n    19\t## Verification Gates\n    20\t\n    21\t- Story gate: `pnpm verify` — source: package scripts (packages/lhc/package.json). Candidates considered: `verify`, `green-verify` (adds check-test-immutability guard), `verify-all`. `verify` selected per skill rule: prefer plain `verify` during story work because stories legitimately add tests; guarded `green-verify` reserved for hygiene/explicit policy.\n    22\t- Epic gate: `pnpm verify-all` (runs red-verify + LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1 vitest) — source: package scripts; matches spec-pack Verification sections (`LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1 pnpm verify-all`). Process suite must report `ran`.\n    23\t- Gate working directory: packages/lhc.\n    24\t\n    25\t## Spec Pack\n    26\t\n    27\t- inspect: ready. Shape: two-file (tech-design.md + test-plan.md). artifacts/ created.\n    28\t- Stories in order: 01-message-read-surface, 02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health, 03-view-contents-report, 04-lifecycle-exercise. coverage.md ignored as non-story.\n    29\t- Coverage gate (coverage.md): PASS — all 23 ACs owned, one primary owner per TC.\n    30\t\n    31\t## Retained Spec Notes (compaction-safe)\n    32\t\n    33\t- Epic 04 builds the inspection surface for the LHC SDK (in-process long-horizon-context system for PI CLI extensions; thin CLI for testing/integration).\n    34\t- S1 message reads: listMessages bounds {from,to,limit,includeDeleted} in source-event order; show returns FULL record blocks + owner-reported form states (never view-shortened, never synthesized); deleted excluded by default, auditable, show on deleted = ok+flag, missing id = message_not_found; CLI deep-equal parity. Search deferred post-v1, no placeholder. Strategy: simple-risk-reminders.\n    35\t- S2 inspect domain: overview (identity, event/message/turn/chunk counts, derivation states, view summary or null, boundary + zone tokens; deleted contract; all 5 thread shapes; pure read) + health (owner/kind/state counts via owner report surfaces ONLY — no direct derived_form/work_item reads; failure detail; repair preview = failed∧¬blocked, never executed; queue visibility; rebuild bracket edit→pending→drain→ready). Read-only delta helper lands here, wraps S1 ops retroactively. Mutation-in-flight fixture via production mutate + partial drain, never hand-written rows. Strategy: tdd-lite.\n    36\t- S3 view report: threadView.describe = stored snapshot only (null when absent, never recompute); inspect.view = describe + measured pull tail; governing contract loadCost.total == actual pull served content (incl. never-compacted: meta null, bands [], tail-only). No new storage/migration. Strategy: tdd-lite.\n    37\t- S4 lifecycle capstone: test/fixtures/lifecycle.ts scripted PI-extension order (create→intake→drain→status→compact→pull→inspect→edit+delete→rebuild drain→health→compact2→pull→materialize); deterministic provider only, zero network; replay byte-identical; SDK teardown/recreate continuity; spawned-CLI checkpoint parity; receipt-vs-health cross-check. Process suite must report ran, never silently skip. Strategy: full-staged-risk.\n    38\t- Test plan: ~26 default tests across messages-read/inspect-overview/inspect-view/inspect-health/lifecycle + cli-process-inspect (process: TC-3.4, TC-5.4). Architecture-risk: read-only delta assert on every new op; throwing-provider suite-wide assert; loadCost parity two independent measurements; check-boundaries + source check against raw SQL into other domains from domains/inspect/**.\n    39\t\n    40\t## Operating Reminders\n    41\t\n    42\t- Impl-lead owns acceptance, final gates, fix routing, recovery. CLI never accepts.\n    43\t- Story cycle: story-orchestrate validate → run (background) → monitor via runtime progress artifacts + 5-min Monitor cadence → review final package → run story gate myself → receipt → advance.\n    44\t- Receipt before acceptance: implementor evidence, verifier evidence, gate result, dispositions, baseline before/after.\n    45\t- Cumulative baseline tracking: total test count must not regress story-over-story.\n    46\t\n    47\t## Cumulative Baseline\n    48\t\n    49\t- Pre-run baseline (2026-06-12, before Story 1): `pnpm verify` PASS — 290 tests / 27 files.\n    50\t\n    51\t## Receipt — Story 01: Message Read Surface (ACCEPTED 2026-06-12)\n    52\t\n    53\t- Story: 01-message-read-surface — Story 1: Message Read Surface.\n    54\t- Story-lead: story-orchestrate run-001 (codex gpt-5.5). Implementor claude-code session 92b30fef-4ad7-45bb-a8e9-4c6f66be56bf; verifier codex session 019ebbeb-f784-77a0-a830-b64185caa03f.\n    55\t- Implementor evidence: artifacts/01-message-read-surface/003-implementor.json.\n    56\t- Verifier evidence: 004/006/010/011-verify.json; final verifier outcome PASS, no open findings.\n    57\t- Findings dispositions: SV-01-001 fixed (under ruling-023 strict-read-purity); SV-01-002 fixed (bounded listing window scoping); SV-01-003 fixed (process gate); SV-01-004 fixed (red-manifest refresh); SV-01-005 fixed (process-suite timeout floor).\n    58\t- Rulings: ruling-023 = strict-read-purity-supersedes-first-touch-recovery (impl-lead, spec-backed). Spec-deviation ruling = APPROVE additive `invalid_bounds` caller_error code (test plan pins from>to → caller_error; Epic 03 additive-codes precedent). Note: story-lead runtime loop never flipped deviation approvalStatus despite 3 recorded approvals (rulings 001-003 in story-lead/); impl-lead exercised run-level acceptance authority directly per operating model. Runtime defect noted as tooling risk, not story risk.\n    59\t- Gates run by impl-lead: `pnpm verify` PASS (300 tests / default suite); `pnpm verify-all` PASS (337 tests incl. process suite ran). Story-lead had additionally reported `pnpm run green-verify` PASS.\n    60\t- Baseline: before 290 → after 300 (default suite). No regression.\n    61\t- Open risks: none story-scoped.\n    62\t- Commit: story-scoped changes committed (see Transitions).\n    63\t\n    64\t## Story Sequence Status\n    65\t\n    66\t| Story | Status |\n    67\t|---|---|\n    68\t| 01-message-read-surface | ACCEPTED |\n    69\t| 02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health | pending |\n    70\t| 03-view-contents-report | pending |\n    71\t| 04-lifecycle-exercise | pending |\n    72\t\n    73\t## Transitions\n    74\t\n    75\t- 2026-06-12: Run created. State: SETUP. inspect ready; config authored; gates resolved from package scripts.\n    76\t- 2026-06-12: preflight ready (002-preflight.json). Gates persisted into impl-run.config.json by preflight (expected side effect). Baseline 290/27 recorded. State → STORY_ACTIVE, Story 01, phase implement.\n    77\t- 2026-06-12 14:20: Story 01 ACCEPTED by impl-lead. Gates: pnpm verify PASS (300), pnpm verify-all PASS (337, process suite ran). Baseline 290→300. Commit 225b6d9. Receipt above. Note: story-lead runtime kept re-emitting spec-deviation ruling despite recorded approvals — impl-lead exercised acceptance authority directly. Side note: impl-lead accidentally rm'd repo-root docs/ while cleaning a stray wrong-cwd artifacts dir; restored via git checkout (docs/taste.md intact). State → Story 02, phase implement.\n    78\t- 2026-06-12 13:55: Story 01 run-001 terminal needs-ruling (ruling-023, cross-story-contract): strict read purity for listMessages/show vs first-touch catch-up recovery. Impl-lead ruled strict-read-purity-supersedes-first-touch-recovery (spec-backed: S1 read-only drift risk test, epic read-only delta assert, AC-1.4). Ruling JSON at artifacts/01-message-read-surface/ruling-023-response.json; resumed with ruling. Verifier had reported pnpm verify and verify-all passing post quick-fix; green-verify failed only on stale red-manifest (SV-01-004) — routed to quick-fix after ruling.\n    79\t- 2026-06-12 13:23: Session restart. Story 01 run-001 found interrupted mid quick-fix (verifier had returned revise w/ 3 blocking findings; implementor session claude 92b30fef…, verifier session codex 019ebbeb…). Background process dead; resumed via story-orchestrate resume from durable checkpoint. Stray artifacts dir at repo root (wrong-cwd status call) removed.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_48","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/03-view-contents-report.md | sed -n '1,170p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Story 3: View-Contents Report\n     2\t\n     3\t### Summary\n     4\t<!-- Jira: Summary field -->\n     5\tExpose the stored active view through `threadView.describe` and report view contents with load-cost parity to `pull`.\n     6\t\n     7\t### Description\n     8\t<!-- Jira: Description field -->\n     9\t**User Profile:** The operator audits what the agent actually saw; agents inside a harness use the same read mid-task.\n    10\t\n    11\t**Objective:** Report stored view bands, gaps, provenance, tail cost, and total load cost without recomputing the view.\n    12\t\n    13\t**Scope In:** `threadView.describe`, `inspect.view`, `lhc inspect view`, stored snapshot reporting, tail cost as served, load-cost equality with `pull`.\n    14\t\n    15\t**Scope Out:** No view derivation, repair, mutation, provider invocation, or direct inspect-domain reads of `thread_view` tables.\n    16\t\n    17\t**Dependencies:** Epic 03 Stories 0-2 landed for view storage and `pull`; Story 2 inspect surface conventions available.\n    18\t\n    19\t### Acceptance Criteria\n    20\t<!-- Jira: Acceptance Criteria field -->\n    21\t- **AC-2.1**: The report names the active view — viewId, createdAt, profile name and resolved config, compactPoint, coveredFrom — and lists every band entry in served order (brief → detailed → smooth): subject kind and id, form used, degraded flag; plus every gap with its reason; plus per-band stored token counts. All of it from the stored snapshot, not recomputed.\n    22\t\n    23\t- **AC-2.2**: The tail section reports message count and token cost *as currently served*: tool results at-or-behind the visibility boundary are costed at their short form, everything else full.\n    24\t\n    25\t- **AC-2.3**: `loadCost` totals what `pull` serves now — bands plus tail — and a test asserts equality against an actual pull's measured content. The report never disagrees with the surface it describes.\n    26\t\n    27\t- **AC-2.4**: A never-compacted thread reports view: null with a tail-only loadCost under the same equality contract (the whole record served as tail).\n    28\t\n    29\t- **AC-2.5**: The report carries the view's recorded source-state provenance (what the compact saw: max event order, form counts) and is a pure read under AC-1.4's contract.\n    30\t\n    31\t- **TC-2.1** (AC-2.1, AC-2.5): On a compacted fixture with one degraded entry and one gap → report matches the stored arrangement exactly: subjects, forms used, degraded flags, gap reasons, band token counts, config, provenance.\n    32\t\n    33\t- **TC-2.2** (AC-2.2, AC-2.3): On a boundary-advanced fixture → tail cost counts short forms short; `loadCost.total` equals the token measure of an actual `pull`'s messages using the same estimator.\n    34\t\n    35\t- **TC-2.3** (AC-2.4): Never-compacted thread → view null, tail spans the record, cost-parity assertion holds.\n    36\t\n    37\t### Technical Design\n    38\t<!-- Jira: Technical Notes or sub-section of Description -->\n    39\t#### Architecture Context\n    40\t\n    41\tThis story adds the single thread-view surface Epic 04 needs: `threadView.describe`. It exposes the stored active view row from the owning domain so inspect never reads thread-view tables directly.\n    42\t\n    43\t`inspect.view` combines `describe` and `pull`. The stored arrangement, gaps, config, stored band tokens, and source-state provenance come from `describe`; tail cost comes from measured pull output, making load-cost parity structural.\n    44\t\n    45\t#### Build Strategy\n    46\t\n    47\tStrategy: tdd-lite\n    48\t\n    49\tReason:\n    50\t- The story has one governing contract, but `loadCost` can drift if implementers reimplement pull selection or boundary-aware shortening.\n    51\t\n    52\tRisk Reminders:\n    53\t- `describe` must return the stored snapshot, not recompute it.\n    54\t- Never-compacted threads return `meta: null`, empty bands, and tail-only cost.\n    55\t- `inspect.view` inherits served tail behavior from `pull`.\n    56\t\n    57\t#### Implementation Targets\n    58\t\n    59\t| Area | Files / Modules |\n    60\t|------|-----------------|\n    61\t| Thread-view surface | `src/domains/thread-view/index.ts` |\n    62\t| Inspect internals | `src/domains/inspect/internal/view-report.ts` |\n    63\t| Inspect surface | `src/domains/inspect/index.ts` |\n    64\t| Shared shapes | `src/shared/inspect.ts` |\n    65\t| CLI/SDK | `src/cli/inspect.ts`, `src/sdk.ts` |\n    66\t| Tests | `test/inspect-view.test.ts` |\n    67\t\n    68\t#### Design References\n    69\t\n    70\t- [tech-design.md §Spec Validation](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:12), lines 12-22\n    71\t- [tech-design.md §Module Boundaries](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:54), lines 54-98\n    72\t- [tech-design.md §Storage](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:100), lines 100-102\n    73\t- [tech-design.md §Flow 2: View Contents Report](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:125), lines 125-137\n    74\t- [tech-design.md §Interface Definitions](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:151), lines 151-213\n    75\t- [test-plan.md §TC → Test Mapping](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md:20), lines 20-40\n    76\t- [test-plan.md §Architecture-Risk Tests](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md:42), lines 42-50\n    77\t- [test-plan.md §Chunk Red/Green Detail](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md:56), lines 56-64\n    78\t\n    79\t#### Test Mapping\n    80\t\n    81\t| TC | Test File / Check | Test Description |\n    82\t|----|-------------------|------------------|\n    83\t| TC-2.1 | `test/inspect-view.test.ts :: arrangement fidelity` | Report entries, forms, degraded flags, gap reasons, config, and provenance equal `describe` output and stored row. |\n    84\t| TC-2.2 | `test/inspect-view.test.ts :: loadCost parity on boundary-advanced fixture` | Tail costs short forms short and total equals estimator over an independent pull. |\n    85\t| TC-2.3 | `test/inspect-view.test.ts :: never-compacted` | `meta: null`, empty bands, tail spans the record, and cost parity holds. |\n    86\t\n    87\t#### Architecture-Risk Tests\n    88\t\n    89\t| Risk | Test File / Check | Test Description | Why AC/TC Mapping Alone Would Miss It |\n    90\t|------|-------------------|------------------|---------------------------------------|\n    91\t| Load cost drifts from served reality | `test/inspect-view.test.ts` independent-pull leg | Measure report total against a second pull's served messages. | A report can look plausible while disagreeing with what agents actually receive. |\n    92\t| Inspect reads thread-view storage directly | `check-boundaries` plus source check | Inspect must consume `threadView.describe` and `threadView.pull`. | Direct table reads could pass fixture assertions while violating ownership. |\n    93\t| Describe mutates or recomputes | `test/inspect-view.test.ts` describe legs and read-only delta helper | Null/shape behavior and before/after state equality are asserted. | Stored snapshot fidelity requires source and side-effect checks, not just output fields. |\n    94\t\n    95\t#### Technical Notes\n    96\t\n    97\t- `threadView.describe` returns ok/null for absent views.\n    98\t- `inspect.view` should not recompute arrangement, form choice, gaps, or source-state provenance.\n    99\t- `loadCost.bandTokens` sums stored band counts; tail tokens are measured from pull's served tail.\n   100\t\n   101\t#### Anti-Shim Requirements\n   102\t\n   103\t- Compare report content to stored row data and to independent pull output.\n   104\t- Do not fake parity by sharing a helper that bypasses `pull`.\n   105\t- Do not create new storage or migration to support this read.\n   106\t\n   107\t#### Production Path Proof\n   108\t\n   109\t- Entrypoint: `threadView.describe`, `inspect.view`, `lhc inspect view`.\n   110\t- Registration/default path: `src/sdk.ts` exposes `threadView.describe` and inspect view; `src/cli/inspect.ts` routes `view` to SDK.\n   111\t- Evidence: default-suite inspect-view tests plus process checkpoint parity in the lifecycle story.\n   112\t\n   113\t#### Verification\n   114\t\n   115\t- Targeted: `pnpm verify`\n   116\t- Story gate: `pnpm verify`\n   117\t- Epic/process gate: `LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1 pnpm verify-all`\n   118\t\n   119\t#### Spec Deviations\n   120\t\n   121\tNone.\n   122\t\n   123\t### Definition of Done\n   124\t<!-- Jira: Definition of Done or Acceptance Criteria footer -->\n   125\t- `threadView.describe` exposes the stored active view row read-only and returns null when absent.\n   126\t- `inspect.view` reports stored bands, gaps, config, provenance, tail, and loadCost.\n   127\t- `loadCost.total` equals measured `pull` content for compacted and never-compacted threads.\n   128\t- `lhc inspect view` returns SDK-parity JSON.\n   129\t- TC-2.1 through TC-2.3 pass with one primary owner in this story.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
